       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose looks like it may be an error. 1600 mg four times daily is 6400 mg/day, which is double the 3200 mg/day maximum in the ibuprofen labeling. The single-dose maximum is also 800 mg for prescription ibuprofen, so 1600 mg per dose exceeds that too.\n\nCommon intended orders would be:\n- **800 mg PO QID** (3200 mg/day, the labeled maximum)\n- **400 mg PO QID** or **600 mg PO TID** for lower-dose analgesia\n- **1600 mg PO TID**, which is still above the labeled maximum (4800 mg/day) and would need a specific reason\n\nPlease confirm the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it. If 1600 mg QID is intentional for a specific indication, let me know the indication and I'll add it to the order note."
      }
